Hi Alex - can you explain a bit more what you're trying to do in this analysis? You have burrowing turned on so you are seeing the environment that the animal experiences when underground. The day you're changing is 147, not 269. There's something funny happening because shade seeking is turned on and what happens there is that the animal is put an an air temperature that is the weighted mean of the air temp in sun and shade (weighted by shade level). This is what appears to be causing changes in the relative humidity from what you set it at, which I'll have to dig into a bit more because that shouldn't be happening if air temp in sun and shade are the same.

All the best,
Mike

